  "transcript_source": "captions",
  "transcript": [
    {
      "s": 4.19,
      "e": 6.74,
      "text": "(dramatic music)"
    },
    {
      "s": 6.74,
      "e": 9.17,
      "text": "- [Narrator] In the year 2000, the entire world"
    },
    {
      "s": 9.17,
      "e": 12.16,
      "text": "was shocked by the sinking of the submarine Kursk,"
    },
    {
      "s": 12.47,
      "e": 16.64,
      "text": "tragically killing all 118 Russian submariners on board."
    },
    {
      "s": 17.07,
      "e": 19.6,
      "text": "This maritime disaster marked a turning point"
    },
    {
      "s": 19.6,
      "e": 21.66,
      "text": "in submarine rescue cooperation."
    },
    {
      "s": 23.06,
      "e": 24.46,
      "text": "(bright, powerful music)"
    },
    {
      "s": 24.46,
      "e": 26.81,
      "text": "Just three years later, NATO established"
    },
    {
      "s": 26.81,
      "e": 28.75,
      "text": "an international club of submariners"
    },
    {
      "s": 28.77,
      "e": 31.77,
      "text": "who could go anywhere in the world to save those in trouble,"
    },
    {
      "s": 31.85,
      "e": 36.77,
      "text": "no matter the place, no matter the conditions."
    },
    {
      "s": 41.27,
      "e": 42.74,
      "text": "- We not having any distinction"
    },
    {
      "s": 42.74,
      "e": 44.61,
      "text": "^between save a life or another life."
    },
    {
      "s": 44.61,
      "e": 46.23,
      "text": "^For us is important brotherhood,"
    },
    {
      "s": 46.45,
      "e": 50.08,
      "text": "^for us is important be here and be ready to save a life,"
    },
    {
      "s": 50.4,
      "e": 52.8,
      "text": "whatever countries belongs this life."
    },
    {
      "s": 53.66,
      "e": 54.49,
      "text": "- [Narrator] Being a submariner"
    },
    {
      "s": 54.49,
      "e": 56.85,
      "text": "is one of the most high-risk jobs in the world."
    },
    {
      "s": 57.64,
      "e": 60.44,
      "text": "It's no wonder, then, that all submariners are a family."
    },
    {
      "s": 60.77,
      "e": 62.57,
      "text": "The common challenge is the sea."
    },
    {
      "s": 63.78,
      "e": 65.83,
      "text": "NATO's International Submarine Escape"
    },
    {
      "s": 65.83,
      "e": 68.5,
      "text": "and Rescue Liaison Office, or ISMERLO,"
    },
    {
      "s": 68.75,
      "e": 71.2,
      "text": "is at the heart of this international cooperation"
    },
    {
      "s": 71.41,
      "e": 74.39,
      "text": "and is open to any nation that uses submarines."
    },
    {
      "s": 78.64,
      "e": 81.34,
      "text": "- ISMER organization include 41 nations,"
    },
    {
      "s": 81.34,
      "e": 84.13,
      "text": "and everybody are cooperating to improve"
    },
    {
      "s": 84.48,
      "e": 87.64,
      "text": "this kind of skill, save a life."
    },
    {
      "s": 87.64,
      "e": 89.36,
      "text": "[Narrator] These kind of skills"
    },
    {
      "s": 89.36,
      "e": 92.02,
      "text": "are hard won, and meticulously preserved."
    },
    {
      "s": 92.3,
      "e": 94.38,
      "text": "NATO trains regularly on submarine"
    },
    {
      "s": 94.38,
      "e": 96.12,
      "text": "search and rescue exercises."
    },
    {
      "s": 96.59,
      "e": 99.09,
      "text": "(tense music)"
    },
    {
      "s": 100.79,
      "e": 104.04,
      "text": "- It's really to be trained because save a life"
    },
    {
      "s": 104.04,
      "e": 106.63,
      "text": "and on the bottom of the sea, it's not so easy."
    },
    {
      "s": 107.44,
      "e": 109.52,
      "text": "[Narrator] The exercises also help share knowledge"
    },
    {
      "s": 109.52,
      "e": 112.13,
      "text": "and strengthen the bonds between partners worldwide."
    },
    {
      "s": 113.66,
      "e": 115.96,
      "text": "- The most important value of this exercise"
    },
    {
      "s": 115.96,
      "e": 117.54,
      "text": "that we have a lot of observers"
    },
    {
      "s": 117.54,
      "e": 119.05,
      "text": "come from all over the world."
    },
    {
      "s": 119.32,
      "e": 121.7,
      "text": "More than 30 nations are observing us"
    },
    {
      "s": 121.7,
      "e": 124.13,
      "text": "and working with us in a very close way."
    },
    {
      "s": 127.47,
      "e": 128.96,
      "text": "- [Narrator] It's also a chance to test out"
    },
    {
      "s": 128.96,
      "e": 131.24,
      "text": "the latest technology in underwater rescue"
    },
    {
      "s": 131.24,
      "e": 133.95,
      "text": "from each country, ranging from"
    },
    {
      "s": 133.95,
      "e": 135.93,
      "text": "specifically designed rescue chambers"
    },
    {
      "s": 136.11,
      "e": 138.2,
      "text": "to mini submarine rescue vehicles."
    },
    {
      "s": 145.04,
      "e": 146.95,
      "text": "^- Each system has its own benefits."
    },
    {
      "s": 146.95,
      "e": 149.05,
      "text": "It depends on the conditions."
    },
    {
      "s": 149.46,
      "e": 150.68,
      "text": "With submarine rescue chambers,"
    },
    {
      "s": 150.68,
      "e": 152.98,
      "text": "they're very good at working at shallow water."
    },
    {
      "s": 153.65,
      "e": 156.28,
      "text": "In deeper water and more difficult conditions,"
    },
    {
      "s": 156.51,
      "e": 159.11,
      "text": "then rescue chambers are of limited use"
    },
    {
      "s": 159.11,
      "e": 161.36,
      "text": "and you need to have a proper rescue vehicle."
    },
    {
      "s": 161.9,
      "e": 163.62,
      "text": "- [Narrator] In a real rescue situation,"
    },
    {
      "s": 163.75,
      "e": 165.54,
      "text": "commanders would have a range of solutions"
    },
    {
      "s": 165.54,
      "e": 168.79,
      "text": "to choose from to make sure personnel get out alive."
    },
    {
      "s": 169.57,
      "e": 171.08,
      "text": "And, of course, there's a website"
    },
    {
      "s": 171.08,
      "e": 173.41,
      "text": "where all nations can share information."
    },
    {
      "s": 174.34,
      "e": 176.16,
      "text": "Being a submariner remains one of the"
    },
    {
      "s": 176.16,
      "e": 178.13,
      "text": "most difficult jobs in the world,"
    },
    {
      "s": 178.46,
      "e": 181.38,
      "text": "but today, the international community is cooperating"
    },
    {
      "s": 181.38,
      "e": 185.67,
      "text": "to improve submarine rescue, and NATO is at the forefront."
    }
  ],
